    <content type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Small Agents, Smaller Blast Radius: Controlling What AI Can Do, (Fri, Oct 16th)&lt;/b&gt; — New or updated LLM releases affect tool choices across your entire stack — from IDE copilots to pipeline automation. &lt;a href="https://isc.sans.edu/diary/rss/33430"&gt;Read&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Show HN: Beeline Multiplayer Agent Harness&lt;/b&gt; — Agentic tools are changing how software gets built — worth knowing what's newly available and battle-tested. &lt;a href="https://usebeeline.app"&gt;Read&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Carbon as a first-class signal: Bringing software carbon intensity to OpenTelemetry&lt;/b&gt; — Better visibility into your systems — new tooling or standards that reduce MTTR. &lt;a href="https://www.cncf.io/blog/2026/10/15/carbon-as-a-first-class-signal-bringing-software-carbon-intensity-to-opentelemetry/"&gt;Read&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Show HN: Inherit – Zero to Iac&lt;/b&gt; — Automation and IaC improvements that could directly reduce toil in your delivery pipeline. &lt;a href="https://inherit.virtualbeck.com/"&gt;Read&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Show HN: Gitsu.app – A Linear-alternative built on GitHub Projects&lt;/b&gt; — Expanding what LLMs can interact with — relevant if you're building or using agentic pipelines. &lt;a href="https://gitsu.app/"&gt;Read&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;AI says you’re right, formal methods say you’re wrong&lt;/b&gt; — Design patterns and lessons from production systems — high-leverage reading for senior engineers. &lt;a href="https://stackoverflow.blog/2026/10/16/formal-methods-say-you-re-wrong/"&gt;Read&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;MCP standardized tools. Now we need the infrastructure around them.&lt;/b&gt; — Expanding what LLMs can interact with — relevant if you're building or using agentic pipelines. &lt;a href="https://stackoverflow.blog/2026/10/15/mcp-standardized-tools-now-we-need-the-infrastructure-around-them/"&gt;Read&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
